<!--
    Pre-configured cXML supplier presets shipped with the module.

    Each preset is created with ``active=False`` and ``state="draft"``
    so it sits in the catalog without showing up in default views or
    accepting traffic. To adopt a preset:

        1. Filter the backend list to "Archived" (or browse from the
           kanban with the archive filter on).
        2. Open the supplier you want, unarchive.
        3. Replace the placeholder values for ``from_identity``,
           ``shared_secret`` (and any other ``REPLACE_ME`` field) with
           the values the supplier assigned to your account.
        4. Link your ``partner_id`` (the supplier's existing
           ``res.partner``).
        5. Switch state to ``open``.

    Demo / runboat installs additionally get an active+open variant
    of each supplier under ``demo/`` with the supplier's published
    demo credentials baked in — see e.g. ``demo/fabory_demo.xml``.

    ``noupdate="1"`` so module upgrades don't reset customer changes.

    Community-curated, not endorsed. Each preset reflects the public
    documentation of the supplier at the time of contribution; APIs
    change. Verify against the supplier's current docs before going
    live, and PR fixes here when they drift.
-->
<odoo noupdate="1">
    <!-- ====================================================
         Fabory (NL/EU) — fasteners, fixings, industrial supply
         Public docs: provided directly by Fabory's punchout team
         on request.

         cXML credential model (Fabory uses NetworkId for From AND
         Sender, DUNS for To):
           - from_domain   = NetworkId  (used for both From and Sender)
           - from_identity = REPLACE_ME (your assigned NetworkId
                             buyer ID — Fabory provisions per customer)
           - to_domain     = DUNS       (Fabory's identifier type)
           - to_identity   = 404789992  (Fabory's DUNS — same for
                             everyone connecting to them)
           - shared_secret = REPLACE_ME (your buyer-specific secret)

         Punchout setup endpoint:
           https://www.fabory.com/punchout/v2/cxml/setup

         Demo installs (runboat / sandbox) get an active+open
         override of this same record under demo/fabory_demo.xml,
         pre-filled with Fabory's published "FaboryDemo" /
         "F@bory12" public demo credentials so the tile is
         clickable out of the box.
    ==================================================== -->
    <!-- ====================================================
         Conrad Electronic (DE/EU) — electronics, components,
         technical supply.
         Public docs: provided by Conrad's procurement-integration
         team on request. Conrad routes cXML PunchOut traffic
         through an Ariba-style endpoint host (the
         ``oci.conrad.com`` host serves the cXML
         ``PunchOutSetupRequest``; the ``oci`` segment is
         historical, the protocol is cXML). The customer-side
         credentials packet from Conrad lists:
           - your NetworkId buyer ID,
           - Conrad's own DUNS (the same value for every customer
             — copy from the packet),
           - your shared secret.

         cXML credential model:
           - from_domain   = NetworkId  (buyer)
           - from_identity = REPLACE_ME (your assigned NetworkId)
           - to_domain     = DUNS       (Conrad's identifier type)
           - to_identity   = REPLACE_ME (Conrad's DUNS, from the
                             credentials packet)
           - shared_secret = REPLACE_ME

         Punchout setup endpoint:
           https://oci.conrad.com/AribaRequest.html

         No matching ``demo/conrad_demo.xml`` ships here yet —
         Conrad doesn't publish a public demo profile, so the
         preset stays archived until a real customer adopts it.
    ==================================================== -->
    <record id="preset_conrad" model="punchout.backend">
        <field name="name">Conrad Electronic</field>
        <field
            name="description"
        >Electronics, components, technical supply (DE/EU). cXML PunchOut. Replace from_identity, to_identity (Conrad's DUNS), and shared_secret with the values Conrad assigned to your account.</field>
        <field name="protocol">cxml</field>
        <field name="auto_create_products" eval="True" />
        <field name="url">https://oci.conrad.com/AribaRequest.html</field>
        <field name="browser_form_post_url">/punchout/cxml/receive/</field>
        <field name="cxml_version">1.2.008</field>
        <field name="from_domain">NetworkId</field>
        <field name="from_identity">REPLACE_ME</field>
        <field name="to_domain">DUNS</field>
        <field name="to_identity">REPLACE_ME</field>
        <field name="shared_secret">REPLACE_ME</field>
        <field name="user_agent">Odoo Punchout</field>
        <field name="deployment_mode">test</field>
        <field
            name="image_128"
            type="base64"
            file="punchout_cxml/static/description/suppliers/conrad.png"
        />
        <field name="active" eval="False" />
        <field name="state">draft</field>
    </record>

    <record id="preset_fabory" model="punchout.backend">
        <field name="name">Fabory</field>
        <field
            name="description"
        >Fasteners, fixings, industrial supply (NL/EU). cXML PunchOut. Replace from_identity and shared_secret with the values Fabory assigned to your account.</field>
        <field name="protocol">cxml</field>
        <field name="auto_create_products" eval="True" />
        <field name="url">https://www.fabory.com/punchout/v2/cxml/setup</field>
        <field name="browser_form_post_url">/punchout/cxml/receive/</field>
        <field name="cxml_version">1.2.008</field>
        <field name="from_domain">NetworkId</field>
        <field name="from_identity">REPLACE_ME</field>
        <field name="to_domain">DUNS</field>
        <field name="to_identity">404789992</field>
        <field name="shared_secret">REPLACE_ME</field>
        <field name="user_agent">Odoo Punchout</field>
        <field name="deployment_mode">test</field>
        <field
            name="image_128"
            type="base64"
            file="punchout_cxml/static/description/suppliers/fabory.png"
        />
        <field name="active" eval="False" />
        <field name="state">draft</field>
    </record>

    <!-- ====================================================
         Manutan (NL/EU) — MRO, industrial & office supplies.
         Public docs: provided by Manutan's e-procurement team on
         request (eproc-support@manutan.nl).

         cXML credential model (Manutan uses DUNS for both sides):
           - from_domain   = DUNS
           - from_identity = REPLACE_ME (your assigned buyer identity —
                             Manutan provisions per customer)
           - to_domain     = DUNS
           - to_identity   = 417526183 (Manutan's DUNS — same for
                             everyone connecting to them)
           - shared_secret = REPLACE_ME (your buyer-specific secret)

         Punchout setup endpoint:
           https://punchout.manutan.nl/PunchOutSetup

         Note: Manutan's cXML PunchOutOrderMessage carries no product
         image, so catalog products created from the cart have no image
         (that needs a separate feed / product API).
    ==================================================== -->
    <record id="preset_manutan" model="punchout.backend">
        <field name="name">Manutan</field>
        <field
            name="description"
        >MRO, industrial &amp; office supplies (NL/EU). cXML PunchOut. Replace from_identity and shared_secret with the values Manutan assigned to your account.</field>
        <field name="protocol">cxml</field>
        <field name="auto_create_products" eval="True" />
        <field name="url">https://punchout.manutan.nl/PunchOutSetup</field>
        <field name="browser_form_post_url">/punchout/cxml/receive/</field>
        <field name="cxml_version">1.2.008</field>
        <field name="from_domain">DUNS</field>
        <field name="from_identity">REPLACE_ME</field>
        <field name="to_domain">DUNS</field>
        <field name="to_identity">417526183</field>
        <field name="shared_secret">REPLACE_ME</field>
        <field name="user_agent">Odoo Punchout</field>
        <field name="deployment_mode">test</field>
        <field
            name="image_128"
            type="base64"
            file="punchout_cxml/static/description/suppliers/manutan.jpg"
        />
        <field name="active" eval="False" />
        <field name="state">draft</field>
    </record>

    <!-- ====================================================
         Topgeschenken.nl (NL) — business gifts.
         Topgeschenken support both SecureOCI and cXML PunchOut for
         the catalog; their purchase-order intake is cXML OrderRequest
         only. We connect over cXML end-to-end (mature + one protocol).

         Their published catalog doc is OCI-only, so the cXML setup
         endpoint + credentials are NOT in it: request them alongside a
         SANDBOX account (sandbox.topgeschenken.nl). Fill:
           - url            = the cXML PunchOutSetupRequest endpoint
           - from_identity  = your buyer id (assigned by Topgeschenken)
           - to_identity    = Topgeschenken's supplier id
           - shared_secret  = as assigned
         and set the OrderRequest endpoint (order_request_url, from
         punchout_cxml_order_send) once known.

         IMPORTANT: Topgeschenken require the cart-item identifier echoed
         back per order line as ``SupplierPartAuxiliaryID`` (it carries
         personalisations such as gift-card text). That round-trip is
         handled by punchout_cxml_purchase (captures it onto the PO line)
         + punchout_cxml_order_send (emits it) — no per-supplier code
         needed here.
    ==================================================== -->
    <record id="preset_topgeschenken" model="punchout.backend">
        <field name="name">Topgeschenken.nl</field>
        <field
            name="description"
        >Business gifts (NL). cXML PunchOut. Request a sandbox account and the cXML endpoint + credentials from Topgeschenken, then replace url, from_identity, to_identity and shared_secret. Their PO intake needs SupplierPartAuxiliaryID echoed per line (handled automatically by the cXML purchase + order-send modules).</field>
        <field name="protocol">cxml</field>
        <field name="auto_create_products" eval="True" />
        <field name="url">REPLACE_ME</field>
        <field name="browser_form_post_url">/punchout/cxml/receive/</field>
        <field name="cxml_version">1.2.008</field>
        <field name="from_domain">NetworkId</field>
        <field name="from_identity">REPLACE_ME</field>
        <field name="to_domain">NetworkId</field>
        <field name="to_identity">REPLACE_ME</field>
        <field name="shared_secret">REPLACE_ME</field>
        <field name="user_agent">Odoo Punchout</field>
        <field name="deployment_mode">test</field>
        <field
            name="image_128"
            type="base64"
            file="punchout_cxml/static/description/suppliers/topgeschenken.png"
        />
        <field name="active" eval="False" />
        <field name="state">draft</field>
    </record>
</odoo>
